diff --git a/docs/test-performance/README.md b/docs/test-performance/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6c0fe7b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/test-performance/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@
+# Test suite performance: notes, baselines and plans
+
+Scope of the optimization effort: `spec/models` and `spec/requests` (system and
+streaming specs are out of scope). Run them per directory, never the whole suite
+(it does not fit into the tool timeout).
+
+## Tools (`docs/test-performance/tools/`, opt-in with `--require`)
+
+| Tool | Use | Output |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `fabricate_stats.rb` | Factory profiler: per factory exclusive/inclusive time, SQL and INSERTs per factory, RSA keygens, plus deterministic counters (total SQL, Fabricate calls, real BCrypt hashes, object allocations) | `tmp/perf/fabricate_stats.txt` |
+| `sql_helper.rb` | SQL counts grouped by spec file, normalized statement, first app call site and example | `tmp/perf/sql_profile.txt` |
+| `prof_helper.rb` + `stack_excl.rb` / `stack_self.rb` | StackProf wall-mode dump, cost categories and top self frames | `tmp/perf/stack.dump` |
+| `hook_timing.rb` | Splits example time into before hooks, body and after hooks; request time | `tmp/perf/hook_timing.txt` |
+
+```sh
+bundle exec rspec spec/models --seed 1 --require ./docs/test-performance/tools/fabricate_stats.rb
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --seed 1 --profile 40          # plain timing
+```
+
+Always use `--seed 1` when comparing runs so that the example order is the same.
+
+## Measurement caveats (read before comparing wall-clock numbers)
+
+- The container reports 12 CPUs, but its cgroup quota is `cpu.max = 200000/100000`,
+  i.e. 2 CPUs. The host is shared: during the factory phase the 1-minute load average
+  moved between 3 and 13, and the same commit ran 1.5-2x slower at different times
+  (e.g. `spec/models` at seed 1: 68 s at the start, 115-120 s and 4-7 min of user CPU
+  later on the same code).
+- Therefore do not compare wall-clock numbers taken hours apart. Use the deterministic
+  counters printed by `fabricate_stats.rb` (`DETERMINISTIC ...` line): SQL statements,
+  Fabricate calls, real BCrypt hashes and object allocations do not depend on host load.
+- Profilers add overhead (SQL subscriber, StackProf): use them for shares, not absolutes.
+
+## Baselines
+
+### Start of the factory phase (seed 1, quiet host)
+
+| Group | Examples | Failures | Finished in |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `spec/models` | 1795 | 0 | 1 min 08 s |
+| `spec/requests` | 1877 | 0 | 2 min 33 s |
+| Sum | 3672 | 0 | ~224 s |
+
+The goal for the two groups together is at least 2x faster than this (about 112 s).
+
+### Deterministic counters (seed 1)
+
+| Metric | models before | models after | requests before | requests after |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Total SQL statements | 102,319 | 80,754 (-21%) | 234,381 | 195,267 (-17%) |
+| SQL issued under factories | 90,336 | 68,782 (-24%) | 176,544 | 137,429 (-22%) |
+| Fabricate create/build calls | 9,263 | 6,860 (-26%) | 18,578 | 14,228 (-23%) |
+| Real BCrypt hashes | 2,974 | 97 (-97%) | 4,867 | 4 (-100%) |
+| Object allocations in examples | 32.7 M | 26.8 M (-18%) | 86.3 M | 75.2 M (-13%) |
+| RSA(2048) keygens | 3 | 3 | 3 | 3 |
+
+"before" is the state at the start of the factory phase (including the configuration
+changes from earlier runs, see below). Allocation numbers are per whole group.
+
+## Changes made in the factory phase
+
+1. `spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb`: removed `after_create { Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status) }`.
+   Every `Fabricate(:status)` created a bookmark owned by a freshly built account, which in turn
+   created a new user, keypair and account stats. That was 805 bookmarks in `spec/models`
+   and 1459 in `spec/requests`, and about a quarter of all SQL issued by factories.
+   Nothing asserts on the implicit bookmark: specs that need one create it explicitly (e.g.
+   `account_statuses_cleanup_policy_spec.rb`, `export_spec.rb`, `backup_service_spec.rb`).
+   `spec/lib/mastodon/cli/media_spec.rb` calls `non_interacted_status.bookmarks.destroy_all`
+   to strip the implicit bookmark. It is now a no-op, and that example's assertions are unchanged.
+2. `spec/support/devise_digest_cache.rb` (new): memoizes `Devise::Encryptor.digest` per
+   (model class, stretches, pepper, password) in the test process. Devise hashes the password on
+   every `User#password=`, and BCrypt's cost is floored at 4 (about 1.2-1.5 ms per call), even
+   though `Devise.stretches` is 1 in test. Every local account build creates a user, so the
+   profile showed thousands of identical hashes. Digests are still real BCrypt hashes, so
+   `Devise::Encryptor.compare` works. Only identical passwords now share a salt.
+   Specs that assert on `encrypted_password` change (`registrations_controller_spec.rb`) use a different
+   password, so they are unaffected.
+3. `docs/test-performance/tools/fabricate_stats.rb` (new profiler) and this document.
+
+Test results after the changes: `spec/models` 1795 examples and `spec/requests` 1877 examples,
+0 failures each (seed 1). Other spec directories that reference bookmarks were checked by
+reading them (see item 1), not by running them.
+
+## Changes from earlier runs (present in the working tree when this phase started)
+
+- `config/environments/test.rb`: `config.log_level` defaults to `info` (`TEST_LOG_LEVEL=debug`
+  to get SQL logging back). At debug level every SQL statement is formatted and written to `log/test.log`.
+- `spec/rails_helper.rb`: `require 'test_prof/recipes/rspec/let_it_be'`.
+- `spec/models/concerns/status/fetch_replies_concern_spec.rb`: `ActiveRecord.verbose_query_logs`
+  is scoped to the group with `around` instead of being set globally at load time.
+- `let_it_be` (shared, read-only fixtures) in `spec/models/account_statuses_cleanup_policy_spec.rb`
+  (`#statuses_to_delete`) and `spec/models/notification_spec.rb` (`paginate_groups_by_*`).
+  Earlier notes referred to this file but it was missing, so it is recreated here.
+
+## Where the remaining time goes (factory phase analysis)
+
+Factories still account for most SQL: about 85% of models SQL and about 70% of requests SQL
+are issued while a factory is the innermost frame. Most of it is application callbacks and
+validations that every record creation triggers. Only some of that is controllable from the
+test suite:
+
+| Hot spot | Measured in the baseline (models, seed 1) | Owner / status |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `UserRole.everyone` (`User#role` with `role_id` nil runs `UserRole.find` every call) | ~11.7k SQL (~11%) | App code (N+1). Memoize in app. Not changed here. |
+| Webhook fan-out on every `User` create: `after_create_commit :trigger_webhooks` -> `TriggerWebhookWorker` runs inline in tests and `WebhookService` serializes the event even when no webhook is enabled | ~8.8k SQL (~9%): ~3.4k webhook lookups, ~2.7k admin serializer runs | App behavior. Short-circuit when there are no enabled webhooks. Not changed here. |
+| `Setting.[]` lookups (`Rails.cache.clear` runs after every example, so settings are reloaded) | ~4.6k SQL | Config/app. Needs a careful decision because it changes cache semantics. |
+| `Fabricate(:media_attachment)`: real Paperclip/vips processing of the fixture | ~0.2-0.4 s per attachment, about 5% of models time | Changing the fixture changes asserted metadata. Needs per-spec review. |
+| `Fabricate(:user)` creates 2 login activities in `after_create` | 2970 creates in requests (about 2% of requests time) | Kept: some specs (for example in `spec/lib`) may depend on them. Candidate for a transient opt-out. |
+| `Fabricate(:account)` for local accounts creates a keypair (3 uniqueness queries per keypair) | 2794 keypairs in models | Kept: `account.keypair` is needed by signature specs. |
+| RSA(2048) keygen | 3 per group (only the explicit `Account#generate_keys` path) | Solved by the precomputed keys in `SigningKeysHelpers`. |
+
+## Plan for future runs
+
+1. Start with `fabricate_stats.rb` and the `DETERMINISTIC` line. Compare counters, not wall time.
+2. The remaining factory-level candidates are small (login activities, media fixture). Review them
+   only together with the app-level items above.
+3. Application-level candidates (need an owner's decision, they change runtime behavior):
+   skip webhook serialization when no webhook is enabled; memoize `UserRole.everyone`;
+   review the `Rails.cache.clear` in the `config.after` hook of `rails_helper.rb`.
+4. Re-run the baseline commands in a quiet window and record the numbers in this file
+   (add a new section per phase; do not overwrite earlier baselines).
+
+## Wall-clock results of the factory phase
+
+Wall-clock A/B runs were not conclusive on this host. Two back-to-back pairs of
+`spec/models` (original vs. changed, same seed) gave user CPU of 3m20s vs 2m58s in one
+pair and 4m51s vs 5m17s in the other, while identical code ran 1.5-2x slower over the
+session. The deterministic counters above are the evidence for this phase: `spec/models` has 21% less SQL and 18% fewer allocations, and `spec/requests` has 17% less SQL and 13% fewer allocations. Whether that becomes a 10-20% wall-clock gain needs a measurement in a quiet window (see plan item 4).
diff --git a/docs/test-performance/tools/fabricate_stats.rb b/docs/test-performance/tools/fabricate_stats.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f088d71
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/test-performance/tools/fabricate_stats.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@
+# frozen_string_literal: true
+
+# Factory (Fabrication) profiler. NOT loaded by default; opt in with:
+#
+#   bundle exec rspec spec/models --require ./docs/test-performance/tools/fabricate_stats.rb
+#
+# Writes tmp/perf/fabricate_stats.txt with, per factory name:
+#   * create/build call counts (top-level + nested)
+#   * EXCLUSIVE time (time spent in that factory, minus nested Fabricate calls)
+#   * INCLUSIVE time (including nested Fabricate calls)
+#   * SQL statements and INSERTs issued while that factory was the innermost frame
+#   * RSA(2048) keygen count issued while that factory was the innermost frame
+# Plus (deterministic, machine-load independent):
+#   * total SQL statements, total Fabricate create/build calls, real BCrypt hashes,
+#     total Ruby object allocations inside examples
+# and the spec files with the most top-level factory calls.
+#
+# Overhead: a few clock reads + one AS::Notifications subscriber per SQL. Use the numbers
+# for relative shares; absolute times are inflated slightly. Prefer the deterministic
+# counters when comparing variants on a noisy host (see docs/test-performance/README.md).
+
+require 'openssl'
+require 'bcrypt'
+
+module FabStats
+  STATS = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = { create: 0, build: 0, excl: 0.0, incl: 0.0, sql: 0, inserts: Hash.new(0), rsa: 0 } }
+  STACK = [] # frames: { name:, start:, child: 0.0 }
+  FILES = Hash.new(0) # spec file -> top-level Fabricate calls
+  TOTALS = { top_incl: 0.0, sql: 0, rsa: 0, bcrypt: 0, fab_calls: 0, alloc: 0, example_time: 0.0 }
+
+  def self.now = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
+
+  def self.wrap(kind, name)
+    frame = { name: name, start: now, child: 0.0 }
+    STACK.push(frame)
+    STATS[name][kind] += 1
+    TOTALS[:fab_calls] += 1
+    if STACK.size == 1
+      ex = RSpec.current_example
+      FILES[ex ? ex.metadata[:file_path] : '(no example)'] += 1
+    end
+    begin
+      yield
+    ensure
+      STACK.pop
+      elapsed = now - frame[:start]
+      STATS[name][:excl] += elapsed - frame[:child]
+      STATS[name][:incl] += elapsed
+      STACK.last[:child] += elapsed if STACK.any?
+      TOTALS[:top_incl] += elapsed if STACK.empty?
+    end
+  end
+
+  module Wrapper
+    def create(name, overrides = {}, &)
+      FabStats.wrap(:create, name) { super }
+    end
+
+    def build(name, overrides = {}, &)
+      FabStats.wrap(:build, name) { super }
+    end
+  end
+
+  module RSAProf
+    def new(*args, **kw, &)
+      if args == [2048] && kw.empty?
+        FabStats::STATS[FabStats::STACK.last[:name]][:rsa] += 1 if FabStats::STACK.any?
+        FabStats::TOTALS[:rsa] += 1
+      end
+      super
+    end
+  end
+
+  module BCryptCount
+    def create(*, **, &)
+      FabStats::TOTALS[:bcrypt] += 1
+      super
+    end
+  end
+end
+
+RSpec.configure do |c|
+  c.around do |example|
+    t = FabStats.now
+    a = GC.stat(:total_allocated_objects)
+    example.run
+  ensure
+    FabStats::TOTALS[:example_time] += FabStats.now - t
+    FabStats::TOTALS[:alloc] += GC.stat(:total_allocated_objects) - a
+  end
+
+  # Patch at suite start: Fabrication/Rails are not loaded yet when `--require` runs.
+  c.before(:suite) do
+    Fabricate.singleton_class.prepend(FabStats::Wrapper)
+    OpenSSL::PKey::RSA.singleton_class.prepend(FabStats::RSAProf)
+    BCrypt::Password.singleton_class.prepend(FabStats::BCryptCount)
+
+    ActiveSupport::Notifications.subscribe('sql.active_record') do |*args|
+      ev = ActiveSupport::Notifications::Event.new(*args)
+      next if ev.payload[:cached] || ev.payload[:name] == 'SCHEMA'
+
+      FabStats::TOTALS[:sql] += 1
+      next if FabStats::STACK.empty?
+
+      stat = FabStats::STATS[FabStats::STACK.last[:name]]
+      stat[:sql] += 1
+      stat[:inserts][Regexp.last_match(1)] += 1 if ev.payload[:sql].to_s =~ /\AINSERT INTO "?(\w+)"?/i
+    end
+  end
+
+  c.after(:suite) do
+    s = FabStats::STATS
+    tot = FabStats::TOTALS
+    total_ex = tot[:example_time]
+    lines = []
+    lines << format('examples wall time (sum of example.run): %.1fs', total_ex)
+    lines << format('time inside top-level Fabricate calls:    %.1fs (%.1f%%)', tot[:top_incl], tot[:top_incl] * 100 / [total_ex, 1e-9].max)
+    lines << "DETERMINISTIC total_sql=#{tot[:sql]} sql_under_factories=#{s.values.sum { _1[:sql] }} fabricate_calls=#{tot[:fab_calls]} bcrypt_hashes=#{tot[:bcrypt]} allocations=#{tot[:alloc]} rsa_2048=#{tot[:rsa]}"
+    lines << ''
+    lines << '== by factory (sorted by EXCLUSIVE time)'
+    lines << format('%-34s %7s %7s %9s %9s %7s %7s %6s  %s', 'factory', 'create', 'build', 'excl(s)', 'incl(s)', 'sql', 'insert', 'rsa', 'top INSERT tables')
+    s.sort_by { -_2[:excl] }.first(60).each do |name, h|
+      ins = h[:inserts].sort_by { -_2 }.first(4).map { |t, n| "#{t}=#{n}" }.join(' ')
+      lines << format('%-34s %7d %7d %9.2f %9.2f %7d %7d %6d  %s', name, h[:create], h[:build], h[:excl], h[:incl], h[:sql], h[:inserts].values.sum, h[:rsa], ins)
+    end
+    lines << ''
+    lines << '== INSERTs by table (under factories, all factories)'
+    by_table = Hash.new(0)
+    s.each_value { |h| h[:inserts].each { |t, n| by_table[t] += n } }
+    by_table.sort_by { -_2 }.first(25).each { |t, n| lines << format('%7d %s', n, t) }
+    lines << ''
+    lines << '== top-level factory calls by spec file (top 40)'
+    FabStats::FILES.sort_by { -_2 }.first(40).each { |f, n| lines << format('%7d %s', n, f) }
+
+    FileUtils.mkdir_p('tmp/perf')
+    File.write('tmp/perf/fabricate_stats.txt', lines.join("\n") + "\n")
+    puts lines.first(4)
+  end
+end
diff --git a/docs/test-performance/tools/hook_timing.rb b/docs/test-performance/tools/hook_timing.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d20d913
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/test-performance/tools/hook_timing.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+# frozen_string_literal: true
+
+# Splits total example time into: `before` hooks (config-level and group-level
+# before/let!/setup), the example body (incl. the request and expectations) and
+# `after` hooks. Also reports the time spent inside integration requests (any phase).
+# Per-file and per-directory breakdowns are written to tmp/perf/hook_timing.txt.
+# NOT loaded by default; opt in with:
+#
+#   bundle exec rspec spec/requests --require ./docs/test-performance/tools/hook_timing.rb
+#
+# Overhead: a few clock reads per example and per request (negligible).
+
+EMPTY_ACC = { before: 0.0, after: 0.0, total: 0.0, requests: 0.0, examples: 0 }.freeze
+
+$hook_timing = EMPTY_ACC.dup
+$hook_timing_by_file = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = EMPTY_ACC.dup }
+
+module HookTimingExample
+  def run_before_example
+    t = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
+    super
+  ensure
+    $hook_timing_before_t = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC) - t
+  end
+
+  def run_after_example
+    t = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
+    super
+  ensure
+    $hook_timing_after_t = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC) - t
+  end
+end
+
+RSpec::Core::Example.prepend(HookTimingExample)
+
+# Time spent inside integration requests (get/post/... -> Session#process).
+module HookTimingRequest
+  def process(*, **)
+    t = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
+    super
+  ensure
+    $hook_timing_request_t = $hook_timing_request_t.to_f + (Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC) - t)
+  end
+end
+
+RSpec.configure do |c|
+  c.before(:suite) { ActionDispatch::Integration::Session.prepend(HookTimingRequest) }
+end
+
+RSpec.configure do |c|
+  c.around do |example|
+    start = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
+    $hook_timing_request_t = 0.0
+    example.run
+  ensure
+    total = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC) - start
+    file = example.metadata[:file_path].to_s.sub('./', '')
+    sample = { total:, before: $hook_timing_before_t.to_f, after: $hook_timing_after_t.to_f, requests: $hook_timing_request_t.to_f }
+    [$hook_timing, $hook_timing_by_file[file]].each do |acc|
+      acc[:total] += sample[:total]
+      acc[:before] += sample[:before]
+      acc[:after] += sample[:after]
+      acc[:requests] += sample[:requests]
+      acc[:examples] += 1
+    end
+    $hook_timing_before_t = $hook_timing_after_t = nil
+  end
+
+  c.after(:suite) do
+    fmt = lambda do |label, h|
+      body = h[:total] - h[:before] - h[:after]
+      pct = ->(v) { v * 100 / [h[:total], 1e-9].max }
+      format(
+        '%-30s ex=%5d total=%8.1fs before=%8.1fs(%4.1f%%) body=%8.1fs(%4.1f%%) after=%6.1fs(%4.1f%%) requests(any phase)=%8.1fs(%4.1f%%)',
+        label, h[:examples], h[:total], h[:before], pct.call(h[:before]), body, pct.call(body), h[:after], pct.call(h[:after]),
+        h[:requests], pct.call(h[:requests])
+      )
+    end
+
+    lines = ['== overall', fmt.call('all examples', $hook_timing), '', '== by file (top 40 by total)']
+    $hook_timing_by_file.sort_by { -_2[:total] }.first(40).each { |f, h| lines << fmt.call(f, h) }
+
+    by_dir = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = EMPTY_ACC.dup }
+    $hook_timing_by_file.each do |f, h|
+      d = f.split('/')[0, 3].join('/')
+      %i(before after total requests examples).each { |k| by_dir[d][k] += h[k] }
+    end
+    lines += ['', '== by dir (depth 3, top 30)']
+    by_dir.sort_by { -_2[:total] }.first(30).each { |d, h| lines << fmt.call(d, h) }
+
+    FileUtils.mkdir_p('tmp/perf')
+    File.write('tmp/perf/hook_timing.txt', "#{lines.join("\n")}\n")
+    puts lines.first(2)
+  end
+end
diff --git a/docs/test-performance/tools/prof_helper.rb b/docs/test-performance/tools/prof_helper.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3cc4f3f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/test-performance/tools/prof_helper.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# frozen_string_literal: true
+
+# Profiling helper for RSpec runs. NOT loaded by default; opt in with:
+#
+#   PROF_OUT=tmp/perf/stack.dump bundle exec rspec spec/models \
+#     --require ./docs/test-performance/tools/prof_helper.rb
+#
+# Produces:
+#   * a StackProf wall-mode dump (analyse with stack_excl.rb / stack_self.rb)
+#   * a stats file (<dump>.stats.txt) with SQL counts/time per statement kind and
+#     the RSA(2048) keygen count/time.
+#
+# Overhead: StackProf adds ~10-20% wall time; compare relative shares, not absolutes.
+
+require 'stackprof'
+require 'openssl'
+
+$perf = { sql_count: Hash.new(0), sql_time: Hash.new(0.0), rsa_count: 0, rsa_time: 0.0 }
+
+module RSAProf
+  def new(*args, **kw, &blk)
+    return super unless args == [2048] && kw.empty?
+
+    t = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
+    r = super
+    $perf[:rsa_time] += Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC) - t
+    $perf[:rsa_count] += 1
+    r
+  end
+end
+OpenSSL::PKey::RSA.singleton_class.prepend(RSAProf)
+
+RSpec.configure do |c|
+  c.before(:suite) do
+    StackProf.start(mode: :wall, interval: 500, raw: true)
+    ActiveSupport::Notifications.subscribe('sql.active_record') do |*args|
+      ev = ActiveSupport::Notifications::Event.new(*args)
+      next if ev.payload[:cached] || ev.payload[:name] == 'SCHEMA'
+
+      kind = ev.payload[:sql].to_s.split.first.to_s.upcase
+      kind = ev.payload[:name] if ev.payload[:name].to_s.match?(/TRANSACTION|SAVEPOINT|RELEASE/i)
+      $perf[:sql_count][kind] += 1
+      # ActiveSupport event durations are already in milliseconds.
+      $perf[:sql_time][kind] += ev.duration
+    end
+  end
+
+  c.after(:suite) do
+    StackProf.stop
+    out = ENV.fetch('PROF_OUT', 'tmp/perf/stack.dump')
+    StackProf.results(out)
+    File.write(
+      "#{out}.stats.txt",
+      [
+        "SQL count by kind: #{$perf[:sql_count].sort_by { -_2 }.first(25).inspect}",
+        "SQL time (ms) by kind: #{$perf[:sql_time].transform_values { _1.round(1) }.sort_by { -_2 }.first(25).inspect}",
+        "total SQL time (ms): #{$perf[:sql_time].values.sum.round(1)}  total SQL count: #{$perf[:sql_count].values.sum}",
+        "RSA(2048) keygen count: #{$perf[:rsa_count]}  total time: #{$perf[:rsa_time].round(2)}s",
+      ].join("\n") + "\n"
+    )
+  end
+end
